--- title A paren as a path segment
--- about `data/(k)` reaches the field named by whatever K holds. It is
--- about the only way a path selects something decided at run time: a
--- about word segment is a name taken as written, so without this a
--- about path can only reach what the source spelled out.

--- id paren-paths/a-path-with-a-paren-is-still-a-path
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
type? first [a/(1 + 1)]
--- result
#(path!)

--- id paren-paths/the-paren-is-one-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Not a nested path, so the length is two and not three.
--- code
length? first [a/(1 + 1)]
--- result
2

--- id paren-paths/it-molds-back-with-its-parentheses
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold first [a/(1 + 1)]
--- result
"a/(1 + 1)"

--- id paren-paths/a-paren-among-other-segments
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold first [a/(b)/c]
--- result
"a/(b)/c"

--- id paren-paths/the-paren-is-evaluated-to-give-the-selector
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [x y]
b/(1 + 1)
--- result
y

--- id paren-paths/reaching-the-third-item-that-way
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [x y z]
b/(2 + 1)
--- result
z

--- id paren-paths/computing-the-name-of-an-objects-field
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is what makes this worth having: the field is not in the
--- note source at all.
--- code
o: make object! [a: 1]
o/(to word! "a")
--- result
1

--- id paren-paths/a-computed-position-past-the-end
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [x y]
b/(0)
--- result
_

--- id paren-paths/a-get-path-selects-through-the-path
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note It is not the path itself, which is what a lit-path would be.
--- code
o: make object! [a: 1]
:o/a
--- result
1

--- id paren-paths/a-get-path-does-not-call-what-it-reaches
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is the whole difference from a plain path: `o/f` calls
--- note the function and `:o/f` hands it back.
--- code
o: make object! [a: 1 f: does [99]]
type? :o/f
--- result
#(function!)

--- id paren-paths/a-plain-path-does-call-it
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
o: make object! [a: 1 f: does [99]]
o/f
--- result
99
